### Kawa Network API - manual test flow
### Requires the REST Client extension. Click "Send Request" above each block.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8000
@farmerId = ad1adf17-3914-48e7-b271-cb0656fe5d1a
@stationId = ffc26103-0e91-493a-848c-ccfbe1d27dce
@cooperativeId = ce70d8f6-e43f-484b-8677-a4e28953f762

### 1. Price schedule (sanity check the server is up)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/price-schedule/

### 2. List farmers
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/farmers

### 3. Register a new plot for the seeded farmer
# Triggers the async risk check - watch the rqworker terminal for log output.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/farmers/{{farmerId}}/plots
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "sector": "Kibeho",
  "station": "{{stationId}}",
  "latitude": -2.598000,
  "longitude": 29.508000,
  "area_hectares": 0.5
}

### 4. Check the plot risk_status
@plotId = 21c8ee74-2640-4762-9471-286597abc426
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/plots/{{plotId}}

### 5. Record a delivery against that plot
@idempotencyKey1 = 3fa85f64-5717-4562-b3fc-2c963f66afa6
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/deliveries
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "farmer": "{{farmerId}}",
  "plot": "{{plotId}}",
  "station": "{{stationId}}",
  "quantity_kg": 35.5,
  "idempotency_key": "{{idempotencyKey1}}"
}

### 6. Retry the exact same delivery (same idempotency key) - expect 200, not a new record
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/deliveries
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "farmer": "{{farmerId}}",
  "plot": "{{plotId}}",
  "station": "{{stationId}}",
  "quantity_kg": 35.5,
  "idempotency_key": "{{idempotencyKey1}}"
}

### 7. Invalid delivery - quantity_kg <= 0, expect 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/deliveries
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "farmer": "{{farmerId}}",
  "plot": "{{plotId}}",
  "station": "{{stationId}}",
  "quantity_kg": 0,
  "idempotency_key": "11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111"
}

### 8. Station delivery feed (paginated)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/stations/{{stationId}}/deliveries

### 9. Export lot including the step 5 delivery - expect 400 PLOT_NOT_VERIFIED
@deliveryId = REPLACE_WITH_DELIVERY_ID_FROM_STEP_5
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/export-lots
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "lot_number": "LOT-2026-001",
  "deliveries": ["{{deliveryId}}"]
}

### 9b. Export lot with no deliveries - expect 201
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/export-lots
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "lot_number": "LOT-2026-002"
}

### 10. Traceability for the lot from step 9b
@lotId = REPLACE_WITH_LOT_ID_FROM_STEP_9B
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/export-lots/{{lotId}}/traceability
